WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.207
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03.257 --> 00:00:05.990
Robotics 101, video 3.

3
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.900
Exploring the hardware.

4
00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.152
Let us open the kit and meet every part.

5
00:00:13.202 --> 00:00:17.170
Each one has a job, and you will learn all of them.

6
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:22.437
This is the Arduino Uno, the brain of the robot.

7
00:00:22.487 --> 00:00:24.897
It runs the program you write.

8
00:00:24.947 --> 00:00:30.720
The USB cable connects it to a computer so you can upload that program.

9
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:36.554
These are the infrared sensor modules, the eyes of the robot.

10
00:00:36.604 --> 00:00:40.959
You need two of them, one on the left and one on the right.

11
00:00:41.009 --> 00:00:44.990
They tell the Arduino whether they see black or white.

12
00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:50.217
The L298N motor driver is like a strong helper.

13
00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:56.217
The Arduino is too weak to power motors directly, so the driver does it.

14
00:00:56.267 --> 00:01:01.133
The two motors turn the wheels, and a small castor wheel at

15
00:01:01.183 --> 00:01:04.050
the front keeps the robot balanced.

16
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:11.326
The battery pack gives energy, and the switch lets you turn everything off safely.

17
00:01:11.376 --> 00:01:15.735
The chassis is the body that holds all the parts, and jumper

18
00:01:15.785 --> 00:01:18.160
wires carry signals between them.

19
00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:22.318
Here is how everything connects.

20
00:01:22.368 --> 00:01:25.841
Sensors send information to the Arduino.

21
00:01:25.891 --> 00:01:29.981
The Arduino sends commands to the motor driver.

22
00:01:30.031 --> 00:01:32.535
The driver powers the motors.

23
00:01:32.585 --> 00:01:36.410
You will wire this yourself in lesson seven.

24
00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.458
Let us recap.

25
00:01:39.508 --> 00:01:42.303
Arduino Uno: the brain.

26
00:01:42.353 --> 00:01:45.395
Two IR sensors: the eyes.

27
00:01:45.445 --> 00:01:49.601
L298N and two motors: the muscles.

28
00:01:49.651 --> 00:01:52.693
Battery pack: the energy.

29
00:01:52.743 --> 00:01:57.270
Next: How an IR sensor sees the line.
